adjudication.rationale:
The new API route `apps/web/pages/api/webhook/app-credential.ts` decrypts and parses user-provided input without any error handling:

```ts
const keys = JSON.parse(
  symmetricDecrypt(reqBody.keys, process.env.CALCOM_APP_CREDENTIAL_ENCRYPTION_KEY || "")
);
```

`reqBody.keys` comes from the request body (only validated as a string by zod). If the ciphertext is invalid, the env key is missing/incorrect (it falls back to an empty string), or the decrypted plaintext is not valid JSON, `symmetricDecrypt(...)` and/or `JSON.parse(...)` can throw. There is no try/catch around this, so the handler will error and result in an unhandled 500 response rather than a controlled 400/403-style error. This is a concrete, verifiable defect introduced by the diff.
